{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Python 3 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Python 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport sys\n\nvar_for_sublime = False\n\nif var_for_sublime:\n    fin = open('input.txt', 'r')\n    fout = open('output.txt', 'w')\n    sys.stdout = fout\n    def give_string():\n        return fin.readline().strip()\nelse:\n    fin = sys.stdin\n    fout = sys.stdout\n    def give_string():\n        return fin.buffer.readline().strip()\n\ndef give_list():\n    return list(map(int, give_string().split()))\ndef give_int():\n    return int(give_string())\n\ndef permutations(arr):\n    if len(arr) == 0:\n        yield []\n    else:\n        for i in range(len(arr)):\n            rest = arr[:i] + arr[i+1:]\n            for p in permutations(rest):\n                yield [arr[i]] + p\n\ndef solve():\n    n = give_int()\n    a1, a2, a3 = give_list()\n    b1, b2, b3 = give_list()\n    mx = min(a1, b2) + min(a2, b3) + min(a3, b1)\n    temp = 0\n    for per in permutations([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]):\n        ta1, ta2, ta3 = a1, a2, a3\n        tb1, tb2, tb3 = b1, b2, b3\n        tmx = 0\n        for el in per:\n            if el == 1:\n                t1 = min(ta1, tb1)\n                ta1 -= t1; tb1 -= t1; tmx += t1\n            elif el == 2:\n                t1 = min(ta1, tb3)\n                ta1 -= t1; tb3 -= t1; tmx += t1\n            elif el == 3:\n                t1 = min(ta2, tb2)\n                ta2 -= t1; tb2 -= t1; tmx += t1\n            elif el == 4:\n                t1 = min(ta2, tb1)\n                tb1 -= t1; ta2 -= t1; tmx += t1\n            elif el == 5:\n                t1 = min(ta3, tb3)\n                ta3 -= t1; tb3 -= t1; tmx += t1\n            elif el == 6:\n                t1 = min(ta3, tb2)\n                tb2 -= t1; ta3 -= t1; tmx += t1\n        temp = max(temp, tmx)\n    print(n - temp, end=' ')\n    print(mx)\n\ndef Hey_Yashwant():\n    try:\n        t = 1\n        for i in range(t):\n            solve()\n    finally:\n        fin.close()\n        fout.close()\n        sys.stdout = original_stdout\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    original_stdout = sys.stdout\n    Hey_Yashwant()\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "```java\nimport java.io.BufferedReader;\nimport java.io.IOException;\nimport java.io.InputStreamReader;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.StringTokenizer;\n\npublic class Main {\n    private static BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n    private static StringTokenizer tokenizer;\n\n    private static String giveString() throws IOException {\n        return reader.readLine().trim();\n    }\n\n    private static int giveInt() throws IOException {\n        return Integer.parseInt(giveString());\n    }\n\n    private static List<Integer> giveList() throws IOException {\n        String line = giveString();\n        tokenizer = new StringTokenizer(line);\n        List<Integer> list = new ArrayList<>();\n        while (tokenizer.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            list.add(Integer.parseInt(tokenizer.nextToken()));\n        }\n        return list;\n    }\n\n    private static List<List<Integer>> permutations(int[] arr) {\n        List<List<Integer>> result = new ArrayList<>();\n        permute(arr, 0, result);\n        return result;\n    }\n\n    private static void permute(int[] arr, int index, List<List<Integer>> result) {\n        if (index == arr.length) {\n            List<Integer> perm = new ArrayList<>();\n            for (int num : arr) {\n                perm.add(num);\n            }\n            result.add(perm);\n            return;\n        }\n        for (int i = index; i < arr.length; i++) {\n            swap(arr, index, i);\n            permute(arr, index + 1, result);\n            swap(arr, index, i);\n        }\n    }\n\n    private static void swap(int[] arr, int i, int j) {\n        int temp = arr[i];\n        arr[i] = arr[j];\n        arr[j] = temp;\n    }\n\n    private static void solve() throws IOException {\n        int n = giveInt();\n        List<Integer> aList = giveList();\n        List<Integer> bList = giveList();\n        int a1 = aList.get(0), a2 = aList.get(1), a3 = aList.get(2);\n        int b1 = bList.get(0), b2 = bList.get(1), b3 = bList.get(2);\n\n        int mx = Math.min(a1, b2) + Math.min(a2, b3) + Math.min(a3, b1);\n\n        int[] elements = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6};\n        List<List<Integer>> perms = permutations(elements);\n        int temp = 0;\n\n        for (List<Integer> perm : perms) {\n            int ta1 = a1, ta2 = a2, ta3 = a3;\n            int tb1 = b1, tb2 = b2, tb3 = b3;\n            int tmx = 0;\n            for (int el : perm) {\n                int t1;\n                switch (el) {\n                    case 1:\n                        t1 = Math.min(ta1, tb1);\n                        ta1 -= t1; tb1 -= t1; tmx += t1;\n                        break;\n                    case 2:\n                        t1 = Math.min(ta1, tb3);\n                        ta1 -= t1; tb3 -= t1; tmx += t1;\n                        break;\n                    case 3:\n                        t1 = Math.min(ta2, tb2);\n                        ta2 -= t1; tb2 -= t1; tmx += t1;\n                        break;\n                    case 4:\n                        t1 = Math.min(ta2, tb1);\n                        tb1 -= t1; ta2 -= t1; tmx += t1;\n                        break;\n                    case 5:\n                        t1 = Math.min(ta3, tb3);\n                        ta3 -= t1; tb3 -= t1; tmx += t1;\n                        break;\n                    case 6:\n                        t1 = Math.min(ta3, tb2);\n                        tb2 -= t1; ta3 -= t1; tmx += t1;\n                        break;\n                }\n            }\n            temp = Math.max(temp, tmx);\n        }\n\n        System.out.print((n - temp) + \" \" + mx);\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        solve();\n        reader.close();\n    }\n}\n```", "token_logprobs": [-0.47589635848999023, -5.960446742392378e-06, -3.7431014789035544e-05, -5.209310256759636e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.006715348921716213, -0.38688647747039795, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -0.018158389255404472, -4.768370445162873e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -1.7881377516459906e-06, 0.0, -1.6689160474925302e-05, -6.556489552167477e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -9.643566590966657e-05, -0.01107910368591547, 0.0, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -0.03231680393218994, -0.1602344661951065, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -9.536738616588991e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.0010562323732301593, -1.2993727978027891e-05, -0.0011712603736668825, -5.006777428206988e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -7.974783511599526e-05, -0.02975643426179886, -0.0024776733480393887, -0.6043670177459717, -1.0132738680113107e-05, -0.0070795160718262196, -0.18911248445510864, -0.5890792012214661, -2.3245540432981215e-05, 0.0, -8.344646857949556e-07, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, -0.1602374017238617, -0.011049510911107063, -8.940656698541716e-06, 0.0, -0.0016946729738265276, -0.00151